  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been (ab)using the newly redone SetPlayerGravity value to create a zero-gravity world (Zero-Gym V2 - https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_36e2f0ee-d694-4f8c-8216-02016be70ddb) and something that'd be really fun to see is if physbones on avatars would respond to gravity changes as well.\n\nMy thinking/napkin coding idea would be to make PlayerGravity a multiplication of the value set in the Physbone, so Physbone gravity is derived by Physbone gravity * PlayerGravity.\n\n(Ie;  PlayerGravity = 1, PhysboneGravity * 1 = Physbone Gravity as it's currently generated.\n\nPlayerGravity = 0, PhysboneGravity * 0 = No Physbone Gravity)\n\nThat way it accounts for the wide variety of avatar settings already in existence, and gives  World creators something to play with and get consistent results even if you set gravity to, say, 0.16 for an on-the-moon world/experience (As some other creators have made)",
